Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO for Windows: CromIKO DNS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The CromIKO DNS screen of the Android app (CromIKO-DNS-Screen.patch and
CromIKO-DNS-Shortcut.patch) in the settings of the desktop version:

- The secure DNS setting (Settings > Privacy and security > Security) is
  named CromIKO DNS, "Encrypt the addresses of the sites you visit".
- The providers say what they filter (blocks ads and trackers, family
  filter, blocks malware, no filtering), and are in the order of the
  Android screen instead of a random one: Quad9, the default, first and
  "recommended", then the ones that block ads, the family filters, the
  ones that block malware and the unfiltered ones.
- "Test connection" checks that the chosen provider answers and shows how
  fast ("Connected • 42 ms") or that it can't be reached.
- "CromIKO DNS" in the app menu, under the Fire button, with the CromIKO
  DNS icon (drawn from the logo by tools/cromiko/gen_feature_icons.py),
  opens the security settings at CromIKO DNS.

